# Copy this file to .env and fill in the required values.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The server refuses to start while any of these is missing.

# A hash of the password you sign in with, never the password itself: make it
# with `docker/bin/yarn hash-password` (or, with the published image,
# `docker run --rm -it ghcr.io/aientech/dossier hash-password`). It's only
# read from here: it is never stored in the database and can't be changed in
# the app.
DOSSIER_PASSWORD=

# Signs sessions and encrypts stored API keys. At least 32 random characters,
# e.g. the output of `openssl rand -base64 32`. Changing it signs you out.
DOSSIER_SECRET=

# PostgreSQL connection string, used by Prisma and the app when run on the host
# (e.g. `npx prisma studio`). Inside Docker, compose.yml points it at the `db`
# service instead. Or an SQLite file, for running without a database server:
# DATABASE_URL="file:/data/dossier.db"
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/dossier"

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Where backups and export files are written (default /data). Relative paths
# are resolved from the app's working directory.
# DOSSIER_DATA_DIR=/data

# How many days of nightly backups to keep (default 14).
# DOSSIER_BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=14

# The usage ping: on each day the app is used, a production server sends a
# random install ID and the version number, once (see Privacy in the wiki).
# Pathfinder: off unless set to on; students are never asked.
# DOSSIER_TELEMETRY=

# Defaults for Settings → AI provider; values saved in the app override them.
# Provider: local (Ollama or llama.cpp), openai (any OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint), anthropic, mistral or lmstudio.
# DOSSIER_AI_PROVIDER=local
# DOSSIER_AI_URL=http://localhost:11434
# DOSSIER_AI_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# DOSSIER_AI_KEY=
# How long one AI call may take, in seconds. Defaults: 300 for a local model,
# 120 for hosted ones.
# DOSSIER_AI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300

# Defaults for Settings → Job search; a choice saved in the app overrides them.
# Source: jsearch (LinkedIn, Indeed and more through Google for Jobs; needs a
# key from OpenWeb Ninja or RapidAPI), adzuna (needs an app ID and key),
# arbeitsagentur (Germany only, no key; unofficial, see below), freehire
# (company career pages, no key) or off. Off until you choose.
# DOSSIER_JOBS_SOURCE=jsearch
# DOSSIER_JSEARCH_KEY=
# Where the JSearch key is from: openwebninja (default) or rapidapi.
# DOSSIER_JSEARCH_HOST=openwebninja
# DOSSIER_ADZUNA_APP_ID=
# DOSSIER_ADZUNA_KEY=
# FreeHire origin; unset uses https://freehire.me. Point at a self-hosted
# FreeHire when you run your own.
# DOSSIER_FREEHIRE_URL=
# The Bundesagentur für Arbeit has no official API: Dossier uses the access
# its own job search uses, without its permission, and its terms of use don't
# allow automated access. Whoever chooses it does so on their own
# responsibility, after ticking "I understand" in Settings → Job search, and
# the job agent never searches it. off takes it out of Dossier altogether.
# DOSSIER_JOBS_ARBEITSAGENTUR=on

# Defaults for Settings → Scoring; a choice saved in the app overrides them.
# ai (the default) scores postings with the AI provider above; jev with Jev
# by TypeSafe, which needs a key from https://console.typesafe.ai/keys and
# gets each posting you score with your profile, without your name or
# contact details.
# DOSSIER_SCORER=ai
# DOSSIER_TYPESAFE_KEY=

# --- Docker Compose ---------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres credentials for compose.yml (these are the defaults if unset).
# POSTGRES_USER=postgres
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
# POSTGRES_DB=dossier
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# --- Google: Gmail and Calendar ----------------------------------------------
# Lets Dossier send applications from your Gmail, read employers' replies and
# offer interview times from your calendar (Settings → Google). Make an OAuth
# client of type "Web application" in Google Cloud Console, with the Gmail API
# and the Google Calendar API enabled, and add the redirect URI
# <your Dossier address>/api/google/callback. Publish the consent screen (In
# production): unpublished, Google stops the access after 7 days.
# You can also enter the client in Settings → Google instead: it's stored in
# the database (the secret encrypted) and overrides these.
#
# Pathfinder: the same client signs students in with Google. Add a second
# redirect URI, <your address>/api/auth/google/callback. Sign-in asks only for
# "openid email profile"; Gmail and Calendar are asked for later, by students
# who turn them on.
# DOSSIER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# DOSSIER_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Pathfinder: how students sign in. firebase (the default once the Firebase
# project below is set): email and password, password reset and Google, through
# Firebase Authentication. google (the default once the client above is set):
# Google only, through this server's own client. code: an email and the access
# code that DOSSIER_PASSWORD is a hash of; anyone who has the code can sign in
# as any email, so trials only.
# PATHFINDER_SIGN_IN=

# Pathfinder: the Firebase project students sign in with. Firebase console →
# Project settings → Your apps → Web app. None of these is a secret.
# PATHFINDER_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# PATHFINDER_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
# PATHFINDER_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project

# Pathfinder: Dossier's job-search tools (Find jobs, Agent, Applications, Inbox,
# the base resume) and their settings. On unless set to off. Off, students see
# the resume analysis, their profile and a short Settings, and the tools are
# closed on the server: their pages answer 404 and their actions refuse.
# PATHFINDER_TOOLS=on

# Pathfinder: the server runs the AI, the job search, scoring and the Google client for every
# student, from the DOSSIER_* variables in this file. Students never choose a provider or enter
# a key, and anything a student saved is ignored. On unless set to off; off brings back Dossier's
# self-hosted Settings, where each user brings their own.
# PATHFINDER_MANAGED=on

# Pathfinder: what this process does. all (the default): serves the pages and
# runs the background jobs (resume analyses, documents, scoring) and schedules,
# as one server. web: serves the pages only; its jobs wait in the database.
# worker: runs the jobs and schedules from that queue. Run one web and one or
# more workers to keep pages fast while jobs run (deploy/lightsail/compose.yml).
# PATHFINDER_ROLE=all
# Background jobs one process runs at once with a hosted AI (default 10; a
# local model always gets one at a time), and per student (default 2), so no
# one holds up the queue for everyone else.
# PATHFINDER_JOB_CONCURRENCY=10
# Database connections one process keeps at most (default 20). Every web
# process and worker has its own pool; together they must stay under
# Postgres's max_connections (100 unless changed).
# PATHFINDER_DB_POOL=20
# PATHFINDER_JOBS_PER_STUDENT=2

# Pathfinder: AI requests each student may make per day on the server's own key
# (DOSSIER_AI_KEY above). The count resets at midnight IST; students who add their
# own key in Settings aren't limited. Unset means no limit.
# PATHFINDER_AI_DAILY_LIMIT=10

# Pathfinder: on the server's own Claude key, the model that reads resumes and
# postings into fields (DOSSIER_AI_MODEL does the review), and the model tried
# once when the first is overloaded or failing ("off" for none). Both default to
# claude-sonnet-5-5. Every call on the server's key is logged with its cost.
# PATHFINDER_AI_READING_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# PATHFINDER_AI_FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# Pathfinder: Startups reads YC's job pages, Hacker News and startups' own
# sites, so it's off unless set to on: no menu item, its pages answer 404, and
# nothing is fetched.
# PATHFINDER_STARTUPS=off

# The address Dossier is reached at, e.g. https://dossier.example.com, for
# Google's redirect. Defaults to the address in the browser.
# DOSSIER_PUBLIC_URL=
